---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE, pageTitle } from '../config.ts';
---

<Base
  title={pageTitle('Mission')}
  description={`${SITE.mission}. MindMotion builds runtime safety software for AI-driven robots.`}
>
  <Nav />
  <main id="main">
    <Section id="mission" heading="Mission" headingLevel={1} class="!pb-8 md:!pb-12">
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg md:text-xl text-accent-2 leading-snug">
        {SITE.mission}
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section
      id="approach"
      heading="Approach"
      variant="tinted"
      class="!pt-10 md:!pt-12"
    >
      <p>
        Capability and trust are different problems. The brain of a robot
        becomes more capable through better data and training. Trust
        does not come from the same place.
      </p>
      <p>
        Trust comes from outside the brain: safety software between the
        brain and the body, holding the body inside limits the company
        deploying the robot has declared, regardless of what the brain
        decides.
      </p>
      <p>
        The brain is free to imagine and evolve. The safety software holds,
        at the pace the physics demands, so safety does not cost throughput.
        We build that software.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section id="founder" heading="Founder">
      <p>
        MindMotion, Inc. was founded by <a
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/david-braun-robotics/"
          rel="noopener"
        >David Braun</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        He has spent more than fifteen years on robot control, the work of
        making robots move safely under constraints, including the control
        of humanoid systems. He holds a Ph.D. in mechanical engineering and
        received the IEEE Transactions on Robotics Best Paper Award for work
        on robot control under constraints.
      </p>
    </Section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
